## 66. Plus One

## Approach:
Start checking the array from the last digit.
If the digit is 9, make it 0 and continue to the left.
If the digit is not 9, add 1 and stop.
If all digits are 9, right becomes -1.
In that case, create a new array of size n + 1.
Put 1 at the first index. Other positions are automatically 0.
Return the new array.

Example:
[1,2,3] → [1,2,4]
[1,2,9] → [1,3,0]
[9,9,9] → [1,0,0,0]

Complexity:
Time: O(n)
Space: O(n) worst case
Normally uses O(1) extra space.

SOLUTION :
class Solution {
    public int[] plusOne(int[] digits) {
        int n = digits.length;
        int right;
        for (right = n - 1; right >= 0; right--) {
            if (digits[right] == 9) {
                digits[right] = 0;
            } else {
                digits[right] += 1;
                break;
            }
        }
        if (right == -1) {
            int[] newArr = new int[n + 1];
            newArr[0] = 1;
            return newArr;
        }

        return digits;
    }
}
